From: John O'Callaghan <johnocallaghan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:37:28 +0100
Subject: media: meson: vdec: reset the VLD before H.264 decoding

The luma of the first H.264 pictures is wrong, up to the second
IDR picture. The error is different on each run. Chroma is correct.

vdec_1_start() resets the VDEC blocks before it powers on the VDEC
memories. Reset the VLD again in codec_h264_start(), after the
memories are on. The vendor driver also does this reset in
vh264_prot_init().

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: John O'Callaghan <johnocallaghan@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_h264.c
@@ -182,6 +182,14 @@ static int codec_h264_start(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 	if (!h264->sei_vaddr)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	/*
+	 * vdec_1_start() resets the VLD before the VDEC memories are powered
+	 * on. Reset it again, or the luma of the first pictures is corrupt.
+	 */
+	amvdec_write_dos(core, DOS_SW_RESET0, BIT(4));
+	amvdec_write_dos(core, DOS_SW_RESET0, 0);
+	amvdec_read_dos(core, DOS_SW_RESET0);
+
 	amvdec_write_dos_bits(core, POWER_CTL_VLD, BIT(9) | BIT(6));
 
 	workspace_offset = h264->workspace_paddr - WORKSPACE_BUF_OFFSET;
-- 
